317
00:26:25.699 --> 00:26:28.131
CTO, CFO, all tech leads.

318
00:26:28.411 --> 00:26:46.736
Context, Bill doubled (1.1 rupees, then 2.3 crore rupees per month) while traffic grew 20%; a third of spend unallocated; fleet sized for festival peak year-round; commitments bought at peak; logs retained hot indefinitely; no way to connect spend to value.

319
00:26:47.016 --> 00:27:07.453
Decision, Cost becomes a tracked quality attribute with owners: allocate 100% of spend (drivers for shared costs, zero untagged), report unit economics monthly, autoscale with calendar pre-scaling, size commitments to the confident floor, enforce data retention by class, and alert on anomalies daily.

320
00:27:08.803 --> 00:27:34.958
Related ADRs, ADR-210 Mandatory tags (owner, service, env, cost-centre) enforced at provisioning; ADR-211 Driver-based shared-cost allocation (L1); ADR-212 Cost per order as the headline metric; ADR-213 60% target utilisation + calendar pre-scale for sales (L2); ADR-214 Commitments at most

321
00:27:35.238 --> 00:27:56.251
confident floor, quarterly ratchet, central purchasing (L3); ADR-215 Retention by data class: debug logs 14 d hot, app logs 30 d hot, then 1 y archive, clickstream 7 d hot, then Parquet in lake (L4); ADR-216 Cost section required in design docs.

322
00:27:56.531 --> 00:27:57.491
Requirements.

323
00:27:58.841 --> 00:28:07.460
R1, Owned. ≥ 99% of spend allocated to a team; untagged spend 1% and reported daily.

324
00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:09.767
R2, Measured in business units.

325
00:28:10.047 --> 00:28:15.017
Cost per order, per active customer and per dark store reported monthly with trend.

326
00:28:15.297 --> 00:28:17.495
R3, No paying for peak all year.

327
00:28:17.775 --> 00:28:27.289
Average utilisation of production compute ≥ 35% outside festival windows, with zero overload during planned sales.

328
00:28:27.569 --> 00:28:29.105
R4, Commitments safe.

329
00:28:29.385 --> 00:28:34.655
Committed spend at most the p20 of the next-12-month demand forecast; reviewed quarterly.

330
00:28:36.005 --> 00:28:37.946
R5, Retention explicit.

331
00:28:38.226 --> 00:28:42.578
Every data store has a retention and tiering policy; defaults are finite.

332
00:28:42.858 --> 00:28:44.565
R6, Fast detection.

333
00:28:44.845 --> 00:28:50.455
A 3x day-over-day cost anomaly for any team triggers an alert within 24 hours.

334
00:28:50.735 --> 00:28:52.143
