336
00:28:56.522 --> 00:29:04.543
Tag policy checked in Terraform CI and by an admission controller; shared costs allocated by usage drivers (L1).

337
00:29:05.893 --> 00:29:08.795
Unit economics (ADR-212).

338
00:29:09.075 --> 00:29:13.405
Cost per order on every team dashboard next to latency and error rate.

339
00:29:13.685 --> 00:29:16.139
Capacity (ADR-213).

340
00:29:16.419 --> 00:29:24.461
HPA at 60% CPU; sale calendar feeds scheduled minimum replicas 30 min before each event (L2).

341
00:29:24.741 --> 00:29:27.195
Commitments (ADR-214).

342
00:29:27.475 --> 00:29:36.392
Central FinOps buys savings plans covering the confident floor; spot only for batch, image processing and async consumers (L3).

343
00:29:36.672 --> 00:29:38.613
Data (ADR-215).

344
00:29:38.893 --> 00:29:47.043
Lifecycle rules in object storage; log levels defaulted to INFO in production; clickstream compacted to Parquet (L4).

345
00:29:48.393 --> 00:29:50.803
Design (ADR-216).

346
00:29:51.083 --> 00:29:57.099
Every design doc states monthly cost, cost per unit and its biggest lever (Ch 32).

347
00:29:57.379 --> 00:29:58.403
Consequences.

348
00:29:58.683 --> 00:30:04.529
Tagging discipline and a small FinOps function; slightly more complex capacity configuration.

349
00:30:04.809 --> 00:30:11.465
Expected outcome: cost per order returns to its pre-migration trend, and spend growth tracks business growth.

